  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "zend_add_helper_SPEC",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_vm_execute.h",
    "description": "The VM add opcode helper calls add_function() with operand pointers that can be invalid/corrupted for this malformed PoV, and add_function_fast() immediately reads Z_TYPE_P(op1)/Z_TYPE_P(op2) (via zval_get_type in zend_types.h) without validating pointer integrity. This causes a wild pointer dereference (SEGV read) at zval_get_type(). Crash manifests in zval_get_type/add_function_fast, but the vulnerable usage is in zend_add_helper_SPEC passing unchecked zval* operands into arithmetic handling.",
    "conditions": "A malformed script/JIT trace must drive execution into ZEND_ADD_SPEC_TMPVARCV_TMPVARCV_HANDLER so that zend_add_helper_SPEC receives a bad TMPVAR/CV operand pointer (not just IS_UNDEF value). The helper only checks IS_UNDEF type info, then calls add_function(EX_VAR(result), op_1, op_2). add_function_fast computes TYPE_PAIR by reading both zval types, dereferencing the corrupted pointer and crashing. Data flow: fuzzed PHP source -> compilation/JIT trace/opline state corruption -> ADD handler with invalid operand zval* -> unchecked type read in add path -> SEGV."
  },
